:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">15</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr></tbody></table>","plainText":"REQUIREMENTS FOR DWELLING UNITS District Requirement Waiver Column A Column B Column C Parking requirement per standard dwelling unit (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an income-restricted unit in qualifying affordable housing (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is qualifying senior housing (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an ancillary dwelling unit (in percent) Maximum waiver (in spaces)4 R1 R2 100 50 10 0 0 R3A R3-1 R3X R4-1 R4B R4A R5A 100 50 10 0 05 R3-2 50 50 10 0 1 R4 50 50 10 0 3 R5 R5B R5D 50 25 10 0 5 R6 50 25 10 0 10 R7-1 R7B 501 12 10 0 10 R7A R7D R7X 501 12 10 0 15 R7-2 R7-3 502 12 10 0 15 R8 R9 R10 R11 R12 403 12 10 0 15"},{"id":"zr-22801-block-004","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">1&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> in R7-1, R7A, R7B, R7D and R7X Districts, the parking requirement per standard <strong><em>dwelling unit</em></strong> shall be reduced to 30 percent where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is 10,000 square feet or less.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"1 For zoning lots in R7-1, R7A, R7B, R7D and R7X Districts, the parking requirement per standard dwelling unit shall be reduced to 30 percent where the lot area is 10,000 square feet or less."},{"id":"zr-22801-block-005","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">2 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> in R7-2 and R7-3 Districts, the parking requirement per standard <strong><em>dwelling unit</em></strong> shall be reduced to 30 percent where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is between 10,001 and 15,000 square feet and waived where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is 10,000 square feet or less.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"2 For zoning lots in R7-2 and R7-3 Districts, the parking requirement per standard dwelling unit shall be reduced to 30 percent where the lot area is between 10,001 and 15,000 square feet and waived where the lot area is 10,000 square feet or less."},{"id":"zr-22801-block-006","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">3 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> in R8, R9, R10, R11 and R12 Districts, the parking requirement per standard <strong><em>dwelling unit</em></strong> shall be reduced to 20 percent where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is between 10,001 and 15,000 square feet and waived where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is 10,000 square feet or less.</sup></p>","plainText":"3 For zoning lots in R8, R9, R10, R11 and R12 Districts, the parking requirement per standard dwelling unit shall be reduced to 20 percent where the lot area is between 10,001 and 15,000 square feet and waived where the lot area is 10,000 square feet or less."},{"id":"zr-22801-block-007","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">4 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>qualifying residential sites</em></strong> in R1 through R5 Districts, <strong><em>accessory</em></strong> off-street parking spaces shall be waived where the number of <strong><em>dwelling units</em></strong> is 75 or less.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"4 For qualifying residential sites in R1 through R5 Districts, accessory off-street parking spaces shall be waived where the number of dwelling units is 75 or less."},{"id":"zr-22801-block-008","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">5 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> existing on December 5, 2024 where the <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> is 25 feet or less, no parking shall be required. In addition, irrespective of the <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> of the <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong>, in R4B Districts, one <strong><em>accessory</em></strong> off-street parking space shall be waived.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"5 For zoning lots existing on December 5, 2024 where the lot width is 25 feet or less, no parking shall be required. In addition, irrespective of the lot width of the zoning lot, in R4B Districts, one accessory off-street parking space shall be waived."},{"id":"zr-22801-block-009","kind":"html","html":"<p>No spaces shall be required on any <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> where there is no way to arrange the required spaces with access to the <strong><em>street</em></strong> to conform to the provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5#25-63\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5#25-63\"><span>25-63</span></a> (Location of Access to the Street).</p>","plainText":"No spaces shall be required on any zoning lot where there is no way to arrange the required spaces with access to the street to conform to the provisions of Section 25-63 (Location of Access to the Street)."}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":22801,"sourcePath":"/article-ii/chapter-5/25-232","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5/25-232","sourceContentHash":"49df0b17d52e195e3781ee6d0d4c3b9ad48fa216f32768cb69e5b28da85fe6de","article":{"roman":"II","title":"Residence District Regulations"},"chapter":{"number":"5","title":"Accessory Off-Street Parking and Loading Regulations","canonicalNumber":"II-5"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[],"tables":[{"id":"zr-22801-table-001","ordinal":0,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"REQUIREMENTS FOR DWELLING UNITS District Requirement Waiver Column A Column B Column C Parking requirement per standard dwelling unit (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an income-restricted unit in qualifying affordable housing (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is qualifying senior housing (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an ancillary dwelling unit (in percent) Maximum waiver (in spaces)4 R1 R2 100 50 10 0 0 R3A R3-1 R3X R4-1 R4B R4A R5A 100 50 10 0 05 R3-2 50 50 10 0 1 R4 50 50 10 0 3 R5 R5B R5D 50 25 10 0 5 R6 50 25 10 0 10 R7-1 R7B 501 12 10 0 10 R7A R7D R7X 501 12 10 0 15 R7-2 R7-3 502 12 10 0 15 R8 R9 R10 R11 R12 403 12 10 0 15","contentHash":"955a5cbde51055a763cd7e68627cc11b4917ddb211c621346875085b0c66059a"}],"mapReferences":[],"appendixReferences":[],"specialDistrict":null,"amendmentHistory":[{"effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","reportNumber":"N240290ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20240290%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Housing Opportunity","action":"Added","notes":null,"description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to expand opportunities for housing within all zoning districts, and across all 59 of the City’s Community Districts"}],"amendmentHistorySourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/ajax/get/amendment/section/22801","effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","lastAmended":"2024-12-05","version":"NYC Zoning Resolution — text through 2026-07-16","researchEligibility":false}}
